# Dev / SCM
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.vscode-test-web/**
.git/**
.github/**
.gitignore
.pnpm-store/**
.smoke-*/**
**/.mypy_cache/**
.DS_Store

# Pyodide caches wheels it downloads into its own indexURL directory,
# which for the desktop host is vendor/pyodide. Those are a local cache,
# not build output: shipping them makes the .vsix contents depend on
# whether anyone happened to run a pandas lab on this machine. The four
# assets the build actually copies are .js/.wasm/.zip/.json, so dropping
# the wheels leaves exactly what esbuild.config.mjs declares.
vendor/pyodide/*.whl

# The command-line package. `esbuild.config.mjs` assembles it beside the
# extension's own output, but it is a separate npm artifact (`pll-python`)
# and the extension never loads a byte of it - shipping it put ~420 kB of
# dead weight in the .vsix, plus whatever tarball `cli:pack` last left here.
dist-cli/**

# Sources & tooling (runtime lives in dist/ + vendor/ + media/)
# The Python wheels are inlined into dist/ by esbuild, so the
# originals do not need to ship as well.
vendor/python/**
src/**
scripts/**
samples/**
out/**
node_modules/**
**/*.map
**/*.ts
tsconfig.json
esbuild.config.mjs
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.vsix
